Calendar view delete (X) button and drag-drop failed for dresses in automatic planning (`planificacion` object). Only manually assigned dresses (`horasConfeccion`) worked. Additionally, dragging part 1 of a multi-part dress left remaining parts in original dates.

## Changes

### Delete functionality
- `eliminarParticionCalendario`: Added early detection for `planificacion` entries, delegates to existing `eliminarPartePlanificada` handler

### Drag-drop functionality  
- `onDropCalendario`: Extended to handle both planning systems
  - Detects `planificacion` entries and extracts all parts across dates
  - When dragging part 1: moves all parts to destination
  - When dragging other parts: moves only that part
  - Persists to `localStorage.planificacion`

### Capacity calculation
- Updated hour counting to aggregate from both `planificacion` and `horasConfeccion` for accurate capacity warnings

## Example

```javascript
// Before: only checked horasConfeccion
if (horas && horas.intervalos && horas.intervalos.length > 0) {
  // handle manual intervals only
}

// After: checks planificacion first
const enPlanificacionAuto = planificacion[draggedVestidoFechaOrigen] && 
                            planificacion[draggedVestidoFechaOrigen].some(e => e.vestidoId === vestido.id);

if (enPlanificacionAuto) {
  // handle automatic planning with multi-part support
} else if (horas && horas.intervalos && horas.intervalos.length > 0) {
  // handle manual intervals
}
```

