Production deployment showed empty database despite seeding attempts, forms failing with valid input, and missing UI for attendance creation. Root causes: seed logic never executed, insufficient error diagnostics, missing UI components.

## Auto-load test data on startup
- Check class count on initialization; seed if zero
- Creates 12 students, 3 classes, attendance records for past 3 days
- Removes dependency on `SEED_TEST_DATA` env var

```javascript
async function initializeTestData() {
    const classCheck = await pool.query('SELECT COUNT(*) FROM classes WHERE active = true');
    if (parseInt(classCheck.rows[0].count) === 0) {
        await seedTestData();
    }
}
```

## Enhanced error diagnostics
- POST endpoints now log request body, validation status, insert values
- Errors include message, code, detail, stack trace
- Schema verification logs table structure on startup

```javascript
console.log('🔵 Student POST request received');
console.log('Request body:', JSON.stringify(req.body, null, 2));
// ... on error:
console.error('Error message:', error.message);
console.error('Error code:', error.code);
console.error('Error detail:', error.detail);
```

## Attendance sheet creation UI
- "New Attendance Sheet" button on attendance page
- Modal with class selector, date picker, notes
- Parallel API calls via `Promise.all()` for performance

## Database schema verification
- `verifyDatabaseSchema()` logs column types, nullability, constraints on startup
- Aids debugging schema mismatches between environments

